WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.400
You were great hosting
"Saturday Night Live."

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.100
Congratulations.
That was fantastic.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.667
Were you nervous going into it?

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:09.501
-Oh, my gosh.
I was freaking out.

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:11.033
On Monday,
I got there and I was like,

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:13.033
"There's no way
I can get through this week."

00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:14.501
-Oh, really?
-And then -- Yeah.

00:00:14.501 --> 00:00:18.000
I mean, no one can prepare you
for that, whatever they say.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.834
Just so much going, you know,
going on

00:00:21.834 --> 00:00:23.567
and coming at you,
and it's terrifying.

00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:25.067
But, you know --

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:27.300
You know, you just have to
make fun of yourself

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.767
and don't take it seriously
and just kind of go with it.

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:31.734
-And at the end,
don't you feel like...

00:00:31.734 --> 00:00:34.400
-And then on Saturday, I was
begging them to bring me back.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.767
-Yeah.

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:37.133
-I was like,
"Please have me again."

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.534
-Yeah.
When you're done, you're like,

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:39.901
"Alright.
Let's do it one more time."

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:41.634
-It's incredible.
It's the best experience ever.

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:44.400
-You mentioned in your monologue
that you're about to

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.767
become a U.S. citizen.

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:47.400
-I am.
-So that's exciting.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.567
-Well, I think so.

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:50.400
The guy, after the interview,
he was like,

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.033
"Yeah, you're approved.

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:53.601
So make sure
you don't do anything

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:54.901
before the oath ceremony."

00:00:54.901 --> 00:00:57.033
I'm like,
"What am I going to do?"

00:00:57.033 --> 00:00:58.300
-Yeah. Wow.
-What?!

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:01.067
-You don't know when the
ceremony is? Or it's soon?

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:03.367
-I do. Next month. Yeah.
-Next month. Congratulations.

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:04.501
-Yeah. It's pretty cool.

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:06.367
-You're gonna be a U.S. citizen.
It's a big deal.

00:01:06.367 --> 00:01:08.868
-Yeah, it's a big deal.
I love it. Yeah.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.167
It's very special.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:11.868
-How long have you been
in the U.S.?

00:01:11.868 --> 00:01:13.968
-I think about eight years.

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:15.901
-Yeah. Eight years.
-Seven, eight. I don't know.

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:17.934
-And New York City
was the first place you came to?

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:19.467
-I did, yeah. This was --

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:22.367
The first time I ever came
to the U.S. was New York.

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:27.267
And this is where I found my --
my little dog, Elvis.

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:29.801
Yeah.
-No way.

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:32.067
-This is where Elvis --
-Elvis is a New Yorker.

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:33.601
-Yeah.
-Yeah. It was meant to be.

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:35.467
-Why did you -- Elvis?

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:37.033
-I was going out and about
in New York,

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:38.834
and I got in the wrong subway,

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:40.868
so I had to go up
to the street again

00:01:40.868 --> 00:01:42.601
to get, you know, downtown.

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:46.701
And he was there in the --
in a window, in the glass.

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:49.501
And I was like,
"That's my dog."

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:56.000
So all my girlfriends went back
to Spain with new bags

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.000
and, you know,
clothes and new fashion.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.400
And I went back with a dog.
-Yeah.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:03.567
And why did you name him Elvis?

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:04.901
-Elvis is -- At the time,

00:02:04.901 --> 00:02:07.434
I was just listening a lot
to Elvis Presley.

00:02:07.434 --> 00:02:08.801
It was what was going on.

00:02:08.801 --> 00:02:11.067
It was my ring phone --
like the ringtone.

00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:13.868
And it was all about Elvis.
-I love that.

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:18.601
Well, it's been such a year
for you because not only "SNL"

00:02:18.601 --> 00:02:21.133
and not only,
of course, citizenship,

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:23.033
but you also were nominated
for an Oscar.

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:25.200
Congratulations for that.
Well-deserved.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.968
-Thank you.
-Well-deserved.

00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:30.701
You were so great in "Blonde."

00:02:30.701 --> 00:02:32.334
How did it feel?
What were the Oscars --

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:34.701
What did it feel like?
Was it amazing? Was it --

00:02:34.701 --> 00:02:36.567
-It was -- It was amazing.
-Yeah.

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:39.267
-It was --
It was also an experience

00:02:39.267 --> 00:02:41.734
that you can only, you know --

00:02:41.734 --> 00:02:44.033
You have to be there
to know what it feels like.

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:45.334
It was pretty surreal.

00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:46.434
-Yeah.
-It was awesome.

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:48.000
-Did you end up
meeting new friends?

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.834
Did you sit at a fun table?
-A lot of people.

00:02:49.834 --> 00:02:51.667
You meet a lot of people --
all these actors

00:02:51.667 --> 00:02:53.400
that you've always been,
you know,

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.334
looking up to
and admiring their work.

00:02:56.334 --> 00:02:59.300
There was one in particular that
I was very, very happy to meet.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.801
-Yeah, and this is Ke.
Ke Huy Quan.

00:03:01.801 --> 00:03:04.100
-Yeah.
-Yeah. Who won an Oscar.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.434
-Who won an Oscar.
Who won everything. Yeah.

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:09.667
-How did you meet him at first?
-I met him --

00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:13.000
I was at the Governors Ball.
-Yeah.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.467
-And he came to me.
And I was by myself.

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:19.434
And I didn't know who he was,
and he asked me for a selfie.

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:22.501
And then, of course, you know,
if you've seen his Instagram,

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:25.334
he posts selfies
with everybody.

00:03:25.334 --> 00:03:27.834
And my boyfriend saw the selfie
and he was like,

00:03:27.834 --> 00:03:29.601
"Oh, my God! You met Ke!"

00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:32.000
And I'm like, "Yeah.
Who are you talking about?"

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.634
He's like,
"He's Data from 'The Goonies'!"

00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:36.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.334 --> 00:03:37.467
-He is!
-And I'm like, "What?!"

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:39.801
-Yeah, I know,
but I grew up, like --

00:03:39.801 --> 00:03:41.834
For some reason in Cuba,
they would play "The Goonies"

00:03:41.834 --> 00:03:43.300
all the time on TV.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:46.734
Like, this was one of my
favorite movies ever growing up,

00:03:46.734 --> 00:03:49.767
and I didn't realize that Ke
was the guy from "The Goonies."

00:03:49.767 --> 00:03:52.300
-Yeah, he was a kid at the time.
Yeah. Now he's a man.

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:54.033
-This selfie was so horrible.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:57.634
I'm so serious because
I'm like, "Hm." I don't know.

00:03:57.634 --> 00:03:59.234
-You didn't know him.
-I just didn't know.

00:03:59.234 --> 00:04:01.300
I didn't get excited.
-But then you saw him again.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.701
-I saw him, and I was like --

00:04:02.701 --> 00:04:05.934
I ran to him and I was like,
"I need a selfie with you!"

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:09.000
-Yeah. Exactly. Right.
-Then I was very, very happy.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.000
Of course.
-Well, I have two pictures.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.634
I have two selfies.

00:04:12.634 --> 00:04:15.300
Here's the one that he took when
you didn't really recognize him.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.934 --> 00:04:20.601
And then here's the one
after you went up to him.

00:04:20.601 --> 00:04:24.434
You're like, "Oh, yeah! Hey!"

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:26.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:26.701 --> 00:04:29.267
-Yeah.

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:31.567
-Let's talk about --
Let's talk about your new movie.

00:04:31.567 --> 00:04:33.701
"Ghosted."
It's with Chris Evans.

00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:36.133
Gosh. He's just fantastic.
He was here last night.

00:04:36.133 --> 00:04:38.133
-I saw it.
-You guys are great together.

00:04:38.133 --> 00:04:39.834
This is your third movie
you've done together?

00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:42.734
-Yeah. Third movie together.
-"Knives Out."

00:04:42.734 --> 00:04:44.567
-Yeah, we met in "Knives Out"
and "Gray Man."

00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:45.968
-"Gray Man."
-And now "Ghosted."

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:49.501
-Yeah. So you've thrown up
on him in "Knives Out."

00:04:49.501 --> 00:04:51.033
You've killed --
You've shot him.

00:04:51.033 --> 00:04:54.100
-Yes. I shot him in the butt.
-Yes. And now you --

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.000
-Threw up on his face.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.367
And in this one,
I'm trying to --

00:04:58.367 --> 00:05:00.567
Well, I kiss him.
I'm nice to him.

00:05:00.567 --> 00:05:02.701
-You save him.
-I save him.

00:05:02.701 --> 00:05:04.934
-You save his life.
-Even better. Yeah.

00:05:04.934 --> 00:05:07.334
-Yeah.
-The idea -- I love it.

00:05:07.334 --> 00:05:09.467
It's basically you guys,

00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:13.200
two beautiful-looking people,
meet, and they go,

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:14.901
"Oh, let's go on maybe a date."

00:05:14.901 --> 00:05:16.934
So they go on a date,
and then you ghost him.

00:05:16.934 --> 00:05:19.467
-Well, I'm working.
-Yeah, but he doesn't know that.

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:21.501
He doesn't know.
And so he goes, "Wait."

00:05:21.501 --> 00:05:23.434
So he got ghosted by you.
He's like --

00:05:23.434 --> 00:05:26.701
But then he realizes that
he forgot that you have his --

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:29.834
-I got his inhaler,
which has one of those.

00:05:29.834 --> 00:05:32.033
-He put an Apple Tag on it.
So he can track you.

00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:34.067
And he's like, "Wait.
I'm going to find out.

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:36.067
Maybe it will be romantic.
She's in London.

00:05:36.067 --> 00:05:37.801
I'll go surprise her
and be like..."

00:05:37.801 --> 00:05:39.534
-Don't do that, people.
Don't show up.

00:05:39.534 --> 00:05:41.701
-Yeah. It's called stalking.
Don't do that. Yeah.

00:05:41.701 --> 00:05:43.400
-Don't do that.
-Don't do that. Yeah.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.968
But he's embarrassed. He's like,
"Alright. I took it too far.

00:05:45.968 --> 00:05:48.267
I texted her too much.
That's why she's ghosting me."

00:05:48.267 --> 00:05:50.133
Then he finds out
you're a secret agent.

00:05:50.133 --> 00:05:51.734
-Yeah.
-You're a spy.

00:05:51.734 --> 00:05:54.868
And you are a kick-ass spy.
You're fantastic at it.

00:05:54.868 --> 00:05:56.767
-I try. Yeah.

00:05:56.767 --> 00:05:58.534
-Yeah. I want to show
everyone a clip.

00:05:58.534 --> 00:06:00.501
Here's Ana de Armas
and Chris Evans

00:06:00.501 --> 00:06:03.133
in "Ghosted" on Apple TV+.
Take a look.

00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:05.667
-I really ate it up, too,
didn't I?

00:06:05.667 --> 00:06:08.367
Especially that sob story
about your coworker that died.

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:10.434
That is low!

00:06:10.434 --> 00:06:13.667
-That was actually true.
Her name was Elena.

00:06:13.667 --> 00:06:15.267
-And she really died?

00:06:18.501 --> 00:06:20.934
-I may have killed her.

00:06:20.934 --> 00:06:23.133
-What?!

00:06:23.133 --> 00:06:26.934
-She was an enemy agent.
She worked for these guys.

00:06:26.934 --> 00:06:28.868
-You said she was a co-worker.

00:06:28.868 --> 00:06:30.467
-She was -- in a loose sense.

00:06:30.467 --> 00:06:32.100
-See, this is what
I'm talking about.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:33.734
It's just lies and lies
and more lies.

00:06:33.734 --> 00:06:35.400
-It's no lies and more lies.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:37.667
It's the sub-lie
of the first original lie.

00:06:37.667 --> 00:06:39.234
-You're unbelievable.

00:06:39.234 --> 00:06:40.634
-Yeah, that's right.

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:43.200
"Ghosted." Ana de Armas.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:45.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:45.501 --> 00:06:48.734
Last time you were here,

00:06:48.734 --> 00:06:51.300
you were talking about how one
of your favorite ice creams

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:54.200
is my ice cream,
which is The Tonight Dough.

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:58.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.167
And so I loved that so much.

00:07:00.167 --> 00:07:02.634
And that's why I wanted
to celebrate your big year

00:07:02.634 --> 00:07:04.367
by maybe having
a spoonful together.

00:07:04.367 --> 00:07:07.968
-Listen. If you give me ice
cream every time I come here...

00:07:07.968 --> 00:07:09.400
-But wait.
I'm gonna do one better.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:11.634
Because you said, actually,
if you wanted to change

00:07:11.634 --> 00:07:13.667
the flavor, we were like,
"What would you do?"

00:07:13.667 --> 00:07:15.267
You go,
"Maybe I'd add a little..."

00:07:15.267 --> 00:07:17.033
-Condensed milk.
-Condensed milk.

00:07:17.033 --> 00:07:18.868
Well, our friends at
Ben &amp; Jerry's heard this

00:07:18.868 --> 00:07:21.767
and wanted to send you
a message. Take a look.

00:07:21.767 --> 00:07:24.100
-Hi, Ana. I'm Ben.
-I'm Jerry.

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:26.667
-We were so excited to hear

00:07:26.667 --> 00:07:29.200
that Ben &amp; Jerry's
The Tonight Dough

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:30.634
is your favorite ice cream.

00:07:30.634 --> 00:07:33.400
-We love that you're a fan
and came up

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:37.434
with something in our kitchen
for a special one-day-only,

00:07:37.434 --> 00:07:39.801
one-time-only surprise.

00:07:39.801 --> 00:07:43.667
-Jimmy, can you show Ana
what we come up with?

00:07:43.667 --> 00:07:45.234
-Since it was
a dream of yours...

00:07:45.234 --> 00:07:47.267
-You're kidding.
-...to have your own flavor,

00:07:47.267 --> 00:07:49.400
we like to make dreams
come true.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.367
Here's your special
one-time-only

00:07:52.367 --> 00:07:54.934
Ana de ArMAS Leche.

00:07:54.934 --> 00:07:57.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:57.968 --> 00:08:01.901
-Oh, my God!
-Come on! I'm not kidding!

00:08:01.901 --> 00:08:05.300
You got to try it.
It's condensed milk.

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:07.868
It's condensed milk
in the ice cream.

00:08:07.868 --> 00:08:09.667
Here's the recipe
on how to make it.

00:08:09.667 --> 00:08:12.133
That's your condensed milk
right in the middle there.

00:08:12.133 --> 00:08:13.767
Oh, my God.

00:08:13.767 --> 00:08:15.200
-You can see it.
Yeah. There you go.

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:16.501
-This is too much.

00:08:16.501 --> 00:08:18.534
-We wanted our studio audience
to join in

00:08:18.534 --> 00:08:21.000
on the celebration, too,
so everyone in the audience

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.067
is going home with
some Ben &amp; Jerry's tonight

00:08:23.067 --> 00:08:26.167
and the directions
to make it are posted.

00:08:26.167 --> 00:08:28.901
Come on! Ben &amp; Jerry!

00:08:28.901 --> 00:08:31.767
Ana de Armas!
Come on, everybody!

00:08:32.067 --> 00:08:34.868
Now, this is like
Pictionary with a twist, okay?

00:08:34.868 --> 00:08:36.000
Now, I'm going to grab a clue

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:38.734
that I have to draw
on your back, okay?

00:08:38.734 --> 00:08:40.267
I'll put a piece
of paper on your back.

00:08:40.267 --> 00:08:42.467
And while I'm drawing,
you try to re-create

00:08:42.467 --> 00:08:44.367
what I'm drawing
on that easel over there,

00:08:44.367 --> 00:08:47.334
while you're
guessing what I'm drawing.

00:08:47.334 --> 00:08:49.434
-Okay.
-Okay? Are you ready for this?

00:08:49.434 --> 00:08:50.601
-Mm-hmm.
-Let's try Round 1.

00:08:50.601 --> 00:08:52.901
Audience, clue?
[ Indistinct shouting ]

00:08:52.901 --> 00:08:55.501
-Wow.

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:56.501
I like that.

00:08:57.934 --> 00:08:59.534
Alright.

00:08:59.534 --> 00:09:02.133
Okay. I think we can do this.

00:09:02.133 --> 00:09:04.133
Alright, turn around.
I will put -- I will put this --

00:09:04.133 --> 00:09:06.234
-Should I get this one?
Oh, I have the big one here.

00:09:06.234 --> 00:09:07.367
-Yeah, you'll have
the good marker there.

00:09:07.367 --> 00:09:10.801
Okay. Ready?

00:09:10.801 --> 00:09:12.400
-Oh, my God.

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:17.434
-Alright, are you ready, bud?

00:09:17.434 --> 00:09:18.868
I think this is
gonna be -- Okay.

00:09:18.868 --> 00:09:21.167
Ready? Here we go.
-Wait. Slow, slow, slow.

00:09:21.167 --> 00:09:22.834
-Yeah. Yeah.
I haven't started yet.

00:09:22.834 --> 00:09:30.901
♪♪

00:09:30.901 --> 00:09:39.000
♪♪

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.534
-Oh.
-Yes.

00:09:42.868 --> 00:09:44.234
How much time?
-That?

00:09:44.234 --> 00:09:46.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yes. What do you think?

00:09:46.133 --> 00:09:47.300
What's your guess?

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:50.234
-Is it a -- It's a --
I don't know -- a --

00:09:50.234 --> 00:09:51.968
[ Buzzer ]
-Yes. What does that look like?

00:09:51.968 --> 00:09:53.868
That's fantastic.
Better than what I drew.

00:09:53.868 --> 00:09:57.367
This -- yours is better
than what I drew.

00:09:57.367 --> 00:09:58.467
[ Laughter ]
I don't know what I drew.

00:09:58.467 --> 00:10:00.734
[ Dinging ]
Lightning bolt.

00:10:00.734 --> 00:10:02.000
-Lightning bolt.
♪♪

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:04.300
-Oh, you would have got that.
-Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

